{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"wifely-allied-discus","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nA serial full-suite run in the subprocess-environment worktree failed after 13,914 passing tests at `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_rich_text_cutover.py::test_cloud_functions_degrade_without_marklas`. The test monkeypatches `rebar_reconciler.adf._marklas` to return `None`, then expects `AdfCodec(rich=True).to_wire(_MD)` to equal `adf.text_to_adf(_MD)`. In the failure the codec rendered a rich heading/list while the direct function returned plain paragraphs. The test passes in isolation, so shared process state or collection/order interaction is suspected but unproven.\n\n## Phase 1 plan\n- Reproduce the failure with a deterministic minimal predecessor/test ordering; compare isolated behavior and capture the divergent runtime identities/state.\n- Inspect the test, codec/function call graph, module caches/singletons/monkeypatches, relevant fixtures, and recent git history without editing production behavior.\n- Build a descriptive evidence dossier, obtain independent falsifiable hypotheses, and run discriminating runtime experiments until one changeable mechanism explains isolated-green and ordered-red behavior.\n- Establish defect legitimacy and perform the bounded caller-dependency gate before any repair.\n- Write the proven RCA and evidence back to this ticket before entering Phase 2.\n\n## Phase 2 plan (only after RCA unlocks repair)\n- Freeze a minimal mechanism-crossing oracle and observe it RED before repair.\n- Keep that oracle held out from the fixer; validate GREEN, exact-defect mutation RED, focused/broader gates, original scenario replication, and sibling/parity sweeps.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A deterministic minimal reproduction or quantified non-deterministic reproduction is recorded.\n- [ ] The isolated working case and ordered failing case are compared with runtime evidence.\n- [ ] Recent history and prior related tickets/fixes are inspected.\n- [ ] A proven, cited root cause and defect-legitimacy/caller-gate conclusion are recorded before repair.\n- [ ] Any repair has held-out RED→GREEN evidence and exact-defect mutation evidence.\n- [ ] Focused tests, lint, typecheck, and original reported ordering pass after repair.\n- [ ] Construct/parity sibling sweep and residual risks receive explicit dispositions.","id":"cbf4-721b-1ce0-44b7","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["debug","rich-text","test-isolation"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Rich-text cutover test leaks marklas state under serial full-suite ordering"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787041162934155001,"uuid":"b94ba207-5443-46e0-bc44-463d402107d8"}